{
 "_about": "Mechanical interfaces of the RobStride actuators, for modelling real screws, holes and bearings. Units mm, degrees. Each value carries its source and a confidence: drawing (maker manual section 1.1 or 2.3), step (measured from the maker's STEP), retailer (none used). null = not published and not measurable, never an estimate. Angles are counter-clockwise about STEP +Z from STEP +X, in each file's own frame; where the output faces -Z they read clockwise when you look at the output.",
 "_method": "STEP read by a small parser written for this job (CARTESIAN_POINT, CIRCLE, CYLINDRICAL_SURFACE, ADVANCED_FACE), run with python -I, with depths from rays cast along the axis through the faces. Not trimesh, cadquery or OCP: trimesh alone cannot read STEP and the other two are not installed. Threads are not modelled, so thread size comes from the drawing and the STEP bore equals the tap drill. All five models are Creo shrink-wraps: interiors are removed, and a flat-floored hole may be cut short where the wrap meets a part behind it. Drawings read from rendered manual pages (pypdfium2 in a scratch folder).",
 "_conflicts": {
  "RS02 hub M4 depth": "drawing 7 min, STEP 6.0",
  "RS04 hub M5 depth": "drawing 6.5 min, STEP 3.5",
  "RS06 hub M4 depth": "drawing 6, STEP 4.7"
 },
 "_missing_all": [
  "output bearing type",
  "bearing axial, radial and moment ratings",
  "screw grade and tightening torque",
  "thread class",
  "mounting-face flatness and hub run-out"
 ],
